{% doc %}
  The shop logo, in up to two versions.

  ## Why both logos are always in the DOM

  A transparent header over a dark hero usually needs a light logo, and the same
  header turns solid the moment the page scrolls. Swapping the `src` at that
  point costs a network request at exactly the moment the customer is looking at
  it, and the header visibly flashes empty while the second file downloads.

  Both images are rendered instead, stacked on each other, and only opacity
  changes. Two files download once, on first paint, and the swap after that is
  free. The stack is also why the header never changes height mid-scroll: the
  inverse logo is absolutely positioned, so it contributes nothing to layout.

  When no inverse logo is set the wrapper does not get `--has-inverse`, the
  stack collapses to a single image, and nothing is downloaded twice.

  ## The heading is only a heading on the home page

  A site-wide logo marked up as every page's only `<h1>` makes each page
  announce itself as the shop name rather than as its own content.

  Parameters:
    inverse (boolean, optional) The template is using the inverse logo

  @example
    {% render 'header-logo', inverse: true %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign st = section.settings
  assign has_inverse = false
  if st.logo_inverse != blank
    assign has_inverse = true
  endif
-%}

{%- capture logo_content -%}
  <a class="site-header__logo-link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}">
    {%- if st.logo != blank -%}
      {% render 'image', image: st.logo, alt: shop.name, ratio: 'adapt', priority: true, widths: '120,160,240,320,480,640', sizes: st.logo_width, append: 'px', wrapper_class: 'site-header__logo-image site-header__logo-image--solid', class: 'site-header__logo-img' %}

      {%- if has_inverse -%}
        {% render 'image', image: st.logo_inverse, alt: '', ratio: 'adapt', priority: true, widths: '120,160,240,320,480,640', sizes: st.logo_width, append: 'px', wrapper_class: 'site-header__logo-image site-header__logo-image--inverse', class: 'site-header__logo-img' %}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      <span class="site-header__logo-text">{{ shop.name }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </a>
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="site-header__logo{% if has_inverse %} site-header__logo--has-inverse{% endif %}{% if inverse %} site-header__logo--prefers-inverse{% endif %}"
  style="--logo-width: {{ st.logo_width }}px; --logo-width-mobile: {{ st.logo_width_mobile }}px;"
>
  {%- if request.page_type == 'index' -%}
    <h1 class="site-header__logo-heading">{{ logo_content }}</h1>
  {%- else -%}
    {{ logo_content }}
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
{% comment %}

